From d9551bb52af0d21e590055f38f09077a2df5d8f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Xiong <daweix3@hermit-03.csl.illinois.edu>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:23:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] mem,sim: Add Protection Unit, PuD-clocked windows and
 model knobs

- Protection Unit (PU): victim-centric disturbance counter with
  mode/distance/N-aware weights; optional double-sided awareness
  (pu_double_sided_aware, "PU-DS").
- PuD-clocked refresh windows: the replay program signals a window
  boundary (m5_work_begin workid 10) and pudWindowReset() clears all
  disturbance and mitigation counters; time_refresh_resets=false
  disables DRAMsim3's time-based reset (harness time is ~140x slower
  than real PuD). SALT-C is not modelled in that mode (warn_once).
- Model factors as switches: tAggOn penalty, SiMRA N-dependence,
  double-sided multiplier, mode-switch synergy, all-zero data pattern,
  direction-aware flips; rowhammer_seed mixed into all flip RNGs.
- PARA counts rows actually refreshed (para_refreshes).
- Per-run rh_mitigation.txt and optional rh_faults.txt fault trace
  (flushed on every write).

Change-Id: I99e483ef6bcf7566dad1971a43a68a0b42ee875f
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
